WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.706
This is a walkthrough of VForce360, the governed
data lakehouse Edgent builds and operates.

2
00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:12.417
Everything you are about to see runs on an open
demonstration tenant with no sign in, so you can

3
00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:18.129
reproduce all of it yourself at acme dot vforce360
dot ai.

4
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:19.750
The data is synthetic.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.890
No sign in. No account.

6
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:29.799
The platform knows this session as an anonymous
subject with read grants over the demonstration data

7
00:00:29.799 --> 00:00:36.709
products,

8
00:00:36.709 --> 00:00:44.750
and every screen you see is what that subject is
allowed to see.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.012
The catalog is the map. One tenant, four catalogs.

10
00:00:51.012 --> 00:01:00.992
Gold carries 29 curated tables, silver carries the
21 conformed tables behind them,

11
00:01:00.992 --> 00:01:09.048
and cedms carries the pages that came out of the
document pipeline.

12
00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:19.750
Bronze, silver, gold and the audit catalog are all
first class objects here, not folders.

13
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:29.462
Open one table and you get the whole record of it.
The columns and their types. Real sample rows.

14
00:01:29.462 --> 00:01:38.437
And the quality tab, which on this table says
plainly that no rules are declared against it.

15
00:01:38.437 --> 00:01:44.436
That is the right answer to give. Absence of a rule
is not a pass, and a platform that hid that would be

16
00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:50.435
worse, not better.

17
00:01:50.435 --> 00:01:56.483
Then the lineage, which is the part that matters for
an audit.

18
00:01:56.483 --> 00:02:03.117
Seven tables, seven edges, and every edge resolves
to the run or the transform that produced it. Nobody

19
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:09.750
typed this graph. It is derived.

20
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.886
Now the analyst.

21
00:02:12.886 --> 00:02:23.527
This is a plain language question against a governed
table,

22
00:02:23.527 --> 00:02:34.169
and the answer comes back as rows, not as prose
about rows.

23
00:02:34.169 --> 00:02:44.449
Ten rows of monthly attendance: the school, the
school year, the month, days possible, days present,

24
00:02:44.449 --> 00:02:54.730
and the rate.

25
00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:02.125
And the SQL is shown. It is always shown.

26
00:03:02.125 --> 00:03:14.750
You never have to trust a number you cannot trace
back to a statement.

27
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:24.382
The follow up names no table. It says what about the
top ten.

28
00:03:24.382 --> 00:03:37.301
The analyst carries the context forward, resolves it
to the same table, and answers.

29
00:03:37.301 --> 00:03:49.605
It also picked a chart on its own, because the shape
of the result is a ranking.

30
00:03:49.605 --> 00:03:55.142
And here is the SQL it actually ran.

31
00:03:55.142 --> 00:04:03.909
Select school id, school year, attendance rate, from
acme gold attendance by month, ordered descending,

32
00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:12.675
limit ten.

33
00:04:12.675 --> 00:04:19.750
That is a statement a data steward can review.

34
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:27.660
The conversation is not a dead end.

35
00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:45.607
Open in SQL Editor hands you the exact statement,
and from there it is your query.

36
00:04:45.607 --> 00:04:52.392
Change the limit, run it again.

37
00:04:52.392 --> 00:05:06.399
Same anonymous session, same authorization path,
same warehouse.

38
00:05:06.399 --> 00:05:19.750
The analyst is a way into the platform, not a wall
around it.

39
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:33.649
This is the compliance ledger, and this is what it
tells an anonymous caller.

40
00:05:33.649 --> 00:05:42.171
Quote: this data is governed. The platform refused
the request before identity was even a question, so

41
00:05:42.171 --> 00:05:50.692
nothing was sent to this browser.

42
00:05:50.692 --> 00:06:00.717
That is the control working, and it is worth being
precise about where it lives.

43
00:06:00.717 --> 00:06:09.615
The refusal did not come from the model. The model
was never consulted.

44
00:06:09.615 --> 00:06:13.750
The platform refused at the door.

45
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:27.688
Access is relationship based, enforced by OpenFGA,
and it is the same decision engine everywhere.

46
00:06:27.688 --> 00:06:37.424
Ask the permissions screen for grants you do not own
and it declines.

47
00:06:37.424 --> 00:06:44.762
Ask for the connector configuration and it declines.

48
00:06:44.762 --> 00:06:54.286
Ask the analyst for a table the session cannot
authorize, and the SQL gate declines before the

49
00:06:54.286 --> 00:07:03.811
query runs, with the reason written out.

50
00:07:03.811 --> 00:07:08.750
Four different doors, one decision.

51
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.607
Governance is not only table level.

52
00:07:13.607 --> 00:07:21.242
Policies and column semantics attach to the object
itself,

53
00:07:21.242 --> 00:07:29.996
so a masking or classification decision travels with
the column into every query, every notebook, and

54
00:07:29.996 --> 00:07:38.750
every answer the analyst gives.

55
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.882
285 scanned pages across 18 batches.

56
00:07:47.882 --> 00:07:56.018
Every page has been read, classified, summarized and
scored.

57
00:07:56.018 --> 00:08:00.222
Look at the disposition column.

58
00:08:00.222 --> 00:08:08.494
The platform did not classify everything and declare
victory.

59
00:08:08.494 --> 00:08:18.122
It sorted its own output into what it is confident
about and what a person has to look at, and the

60
00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:27.750
confidence score is the thing that decides.

61
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.355
This is the gate.

62
00:08:30.355 --> 00:08:38.668
Eighty pages are sitting in a human review queue
right now, each one with the reason it landed there

63
00:08:38.668 --> 00:08:46.981
written next to it.

64
00:08:46.981 --> 00:08:54.185
Segmentation fallback. Low confidence transcription.

65
00:08:54.185 --> 00:09:02.775
A person accepts or reprocesses, and the decision is
recorded.

66
00:09:02.775 --> 00:09:12.750
Nothing crosses from machine output to trusted
record without that step.

67
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.700
And here is where it lands.

68
00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:23.827
The same pages, as a queryable table in the catalog.

69
00:09:23.827 --> 00:09:34.723
22 columns carrying the extracted text, the summary,
the document type, the confidence, the review

70
00:09:34.723 --> 00:09:45.618
disposition and its reason, and a sha256 of the
source page.

71
00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:52.882
The scan is now data you can join to, query and
cite.

72
00:09:52.882 --> 00:10:02.750
The hash is how you prove the row still refers to
the page it came from.

73
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:10.697
Which means you can ask about the paper the same way
you ask about the numbers.

74
00:10:10.697 --> 00:10:15.860
How many pages are still waiting on a person.
Eighty.

75
00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:24.239
That is the same eighty you just saw in the review
queue, and it is not a coincidence.

76
00:10:24.239 --> 00:10:32.131
The queue and the analyst are reading the same
table, so they cannot drift apart.

77
00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:37.440
Same analyst, same governed path, same SQL shown.
There is no separate document product to buy and

78
00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.750
integrate.

79
00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:53.317
Ten flows on this tenant, and the engine behind them
is live.

80
00:10:53.317 --> 00:10:59.945
Records intake, FOIA request intake, 311 service
request routing, grant application triage, a nightly

81
00:10:59.945 --> 00:11:06.572
rollup, a retention sweep.

82
00:11:06.572 --> 00:11:11.750
Triggers are schedules, HTTP endpoints, or manual.

83
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.785
Open one and the graph is not a picture of a
pipeline. It is the pipeline, read live from the

84
00:11:16.785 --> 00:11:21.571
engine.

85
00:11:21.571 --> 00:11:27.541
Collect the day's counters, summarize them, then a
real branch.

86
00:11:27.541 --> 00:11:32.611
If the backlog is healthy, publish to the morning
dashboard. If it is not, escalate to the duty

87
00:11:32.611 --> 00:11:37.680
supervisor.

88
00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:46.114
And here is the run history. Three nights, three
successes, two in the morning each time.

89
00:11:46.114 --> 00:11:53.932
This is the integration surface: a flow reaches a
source through a connector, lands it in bronze, and

90
00:11:53.932 --> 00:12:01.750
the catalog picks the new fields up without a schema
migration.

91
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:08.444
Twenty validation rules across the catalog, 99.3
percent passing, with the timestamp of the last

92
00:12:08.444 --> 00:12:14.888
evaluation on the page.

93
00:12:14.888 --> 00:12:22.299
Data quality is not a report somebody writes at the
end of a quarter.

94
00:12:22.299 --> 00:12:31.750
It is a check that runs against live rows and is
visible to anyone who opens the tenant.

95
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.489
And the results pin to a dashboard.

96
00:12:36.489 --> 00:12:44.119
Built on the same governed tables the analyst
queries, so the dashboard and the answer cannot

97
00:12:44.119 --> 00:12:51.750
disagree with each other.

98
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:58.420
VForce360 is built and operated by Edgent LLC, a
service disabled veteran owned small business in

99
00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:04.841
Bastrop, Texas.

100
00:13:04.841 --> 00:13:10.807
Everything in this walkthrough is running on
synthetic data on an open tenant, and the link is on

101
00:13:10.807 --> 00:13:16.773
screen.

102
00:13:16.773 --> 00:13:23.705
Nothing was staged for the recording and nothing was
sped up.

103
00:13:23.705 --> 00:13:30.750
